There’s a connection to your earlier observation about shadows.

A shadow needs light. And a perspective needs something against which it can be contrasted.

Remove the contrast entirely, and you can lose the ability to distinguish an imagined world from the world you’re actually inhabiting.

That is why I would always preserve the return path. If an exercise starts feeling literally true or destabilizes your sense of reality, that’s a reason to stop and ground yourself, not push further.

